  "id": "Compound::DB01037 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Selegiline is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions involving different target molecules. The evidence suggests that Selegiline may influence Cyp3a4 via its ability to cause the expression or activation of compounds that bind to Cyp3a4. Specifically, Selegiline appears to trigger the release of Budesonide, Azelastine, or Temozolomide, which in turn bind to Cyp3a4. These compounds are all classified as organic molecules or tertiary amino compounds, indicating a potential pathway where Selegiline indirectly modulates Cyp3a4 through the activation of these downstream molecules. The shared lowest common ancestor between Selegiline and these compounds—Organic Molecule or Tertiary Amino Compound—suggests a broader molecular mechanism involving the activation of diverse chemical entities that ultimately interact with Cyp3a4. This integrated pathway highlights the role of Selegiline in influencing Cyp3a4 through a network of molecular interactions, emphasizing the importance of these compounds in the pharmacological effects of Selegiline.",
